--- body ---
## Context
Ticket 0084 fixes the crash/dir-creation bug when --help is passed to a
subcommand. This ticket goes further: make --help a first-class, documented
feature with per-command help strings, so `erg init --help` prints something
useful rather than just the generic command list.

## Actions
1. Add per-command usage strings (one paragraph each) alongside the existing
   `printUsage()` global list.
2. In `main()`, when `rest` contains `--help`/`-h`, dispatch to the
   per-command help string rather than the global list.
3. Document `[--help]` in the global usage header line.

## Test
```
erg init --help   # prints init-specific usage (DIR arg, what files are unpacked)
erg close --help  # prints close-specific usage (ID, REASON, DIR args)
```

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Every command has a per-command help string
- [ ] `erg COMMAND --help` prints that string and exits 0
- [ ] Global `erg --help` still prints the full command list
- [ ] `make test` passes
